      "name": "Pygoscelis",
      "rank": "GENUS",
      "description": "Brush-tailed penguins — medium-sized Antarctic penguins named for their long, stiff tail feathers that brush the ground when walking. They are the most abundant penguins on Earth, with Adélie and Chinstrap colonies numbering in the millions. All three species breed on the Antarctic continent and subantarctic islands.",
