      "description": "The yellow-eyed penguin — a monotypic genus endemic to New Zealand. Distinguished by its pale yellow eyes and yellow head band. Considered the rarest penguin species, with around 4,000 individuals remaining. It is the only penguin with a solitary, non-colonial breeding style, nesting in coastal scrub and forest.",
